    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2Cso4WAZSWbQutHMvcAniFJ)_\n\n## What\n\nThe nightly tidy for the PRs merged since last night: #290, #293, #294, #295, #298, #299.\n\n- **Emacs changelog, feature sets**: #290 in \"Search\", #298 in \"Org tables and dynamic blocks\", #299 in \"Note tags\", #295 in \"Module docs and layout\".\n- **Being developed**: \"sp-navi fails to load\" is gone (#290 merged). The keymap line now includes #294 (CUA dropped everywhere) and the open #296 and #297. New line for the open #300 (file notes into subfolders by tag, remove Denote).\n- **Root `CHANGELOG.org`**: #293 (Stow guide, `STALE=ok`) in the Stow set.\n- **Module docs**: the new \"Changes by pull request\" entries (#290, #298, #299, #295) use the nested-bullet format that #295 introduced.\n\n## Left out on purpose\n\n- #296, #297 and #300 are open and get their feature-set lines when they merge; #296's i3 and sway part will go to the root changelog then.\n- #291 was the previous tidy.\n\nOnly prose changed, no code blocks, so the `tangle` check should be unaffected.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiAhURtzPFib2Qr56NG)_",
